The sum matters, but consider: XP=3 on level=5 sum=8,
XP=5 on level=3 sum=8.  Equal sum means an equal
distribution of monsters being created.  An XP=5
character can handle those monsters much more easily.

Early on I like my XP level to go up before I descend.
This is why.  Exception: I descend stairs immediately
then climb back up.  Again because the monsters at
that time are created based on XP+lev that moment, not
on when I level up and descend again.

At some point XP level and dungeon level stop matching.
It happens somewhere above XP=5 and well below XP=15.

